# Campaign agent and MCP

- `Journeys.Agent` exists to author and manage campaigns — not a second rules engine.
- Keep MCP and A2A wiring in dedicated types; register from `Program.cs`.
- Tool handlers call the same Core services the REST API uses.
- Agent-authored programs must go through the same APIs the engine executes (Draft/Live).
- Governance prompts and checklists are source-adjacent content; do not fork business rules into prompt-only logic.
